Subject: [PATCH] crypto: af_alg: allow async provider for ctr(aes)

Upstream-Status: Pending [validate V851 hardware-provider exposure]

AF_ALG's skcipher recv path submits requests with crypto_wait_req(), so it
already waits for asynchronous Crypto API providers before returning data to
userspace. Allow the asynchronous provider only for ctr(aes), preserving the
existing restrictions for every other algorithm. This lets the V851 sun8i CE
provider serve AF_ALG AES-CTR requests instead of silently selecting
ctr(aes-lib).

---
 crypto/algif_skcipher.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crypto/algif_skcipher.c b/crypto/algif_skcipher.c
index 000000000000..111111111111 100644
--- a/crypto/algif_skcipher.c
+++ b/crypto/algif_skcipher.c
@@ -311,8 +311,12 @@ static void *skcipher_bind(const char *name)
 {
 	u32 mask = AF_ALG_CRYPTOAPI_MASK;
 
+	/* The recv path waits for async skcipher requests to complete. */
+	if (!strcmp(name, "ctr(aes)"))
+		mask &= ~CRYPTO_ALG_ASYNC;
+
 	if (strcmp(name, "cbc(paes)") == 0)
 		mask = 0;
 
 	return crypto_alloc_skcipher(name, 0, mask);
 }
